prompt:
Implement a multi-model 3D scene builder using Three.js. Users can select and place multiple 3D models from a model library to compose a scene.

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Use the following importmap in <head>, and import via ES Modules inside <script type="module">:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>
<script type="module">
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { GLTFLoader } from 'three/addons/loaders/GLTFLoader.js';
import { OrbitControls } from 'three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js';
// Write your code here
</script>

[Model Loading]
(1) Use GLTFLoader to preload 4 models:
  - assets/ToyCar.glb (car)
  - assets/RobotExpressive.glb (robot)
  - assets/Duck.glb (duck)
  - assets/Lantern.glb (lantern);
(2) After loading is complete, display thumbnail buttons for the 4 models in the left panel (id="palette");

[Placement Interaction]
(3) Clicking a model in the panel enters "placement mode";
(4) Display a semi-transparent preview while the mouse moves over the ground plane;
(5) Click the ground to confirm placement and instantiate the model at that position;

[Selection and Manipulation]
(6) Click a placed model to select it (yellow outline or emissive highlight);
(7) After selection, the model can be moved by dragging with the mouse (on the xz plane);
(8) Rotate the selected object with the mouse wheel (15 degrees per step);
(9) A UI slider (id="scaleSlider", range 0.5-3) controls the scale of the selected object;
(10) Press the Delete key to delete the selected object;

[Multiple Selection]
(11) Shift+click to select multiple objects;
(12) When multiple objects are selected, the "Align" button (id="alignBtn") aligns the selected objects to the grid (spacing of 2 units);

[OrbitControls]
(13) Support orbit viewing when not dragging;

[HUD Display]
(14) HUD in the upper-left corner:
  - Total number of scene objects (id="objectCount")
  - Number of selected objects (id="selectedCount")
  - Grid snapping state (id="gridSnap", on/off)

[State Exposure (Required)]
Update window.__3D_STATE__ every frame:
  - modelsLoaded: boolean (all 4 models have finished loading)
  - objectCount: number
  - selectedCount: number
  - gridSnap: boolean
  - placementMode: string (name of the model currently in placement mode; "" means none)

Output a single standalone HTML file.
